The way to specify both the position of the middle of the 0th
selection around the circle, and the radius of the menu, is to supply
as input to the create_menu function an x and y offset from the center
of the menu where the 0th item is to be centered. i.e.:

x=0,y=-40, 2 selections => radius of 40, 0th item is down, 1st is up,
	Yes/No menu.
x=-30, y=0, 2 selections => radius of 30, 0th iten is left, 1st is
	right, 0/1 menu.
x=20, y=20, 4 selections => radius of sqr(20^2+20^2) = 28.28, 0th item
	is NE, X shaped menu.
x=50, y=0, 12 selections => radius of 50, 0th item is up, clock face
	menu.

	-Don


