Take the pi-relative coordinates of the cursor.  These are x and y values
between -1152 and +1152.  Normalize by adding 1152 to each, divide
x by y, (giving an integer between 1 and 2304), and then divide that by
100.  The result is a hash between 0 and 23 to give a first approximation
of which pi is being pointed to.
-mark


