	Menus are indeed a subject of religous war.  One should not decide on
	the basis of what is more modern -- in 5 years, some other choice
	will be more modern.

	The deicions has to be made on the basis of the task, the menu
	requirements, the hardware constraints (especially screen size,
	resolution, and painting speed), and the class of users.

	In szome cases, cascading menus will be superior, in others it will be
	overlapping hierarchies, and in others it will be pie menus (which are
	really what are most modern today -- not that this matters).

