The "uwm" implementation of pie menus I did a few years ago using the
X10R4 version of uwm, which isn't useful with X11 (window managers
were much simpler in the days of X10). I have started work on
salvaging and cleaning up the pie menu related code from the old
pie-menuified uwm, so that it can be used to implement pie menus in
other toolkits. If you really want, I could send you the X10 uwm (it's
messy but it works ok in X10, and I was even able to get it to work
with the X10toX11 protocol converter, but as such it's not usable as a
window manager, since the X11 window managers have many more
responsibilities, as specified in the ICCCM.) It would probably be a
bit of work retrofitting the code into an X11 window manager. More
useful would be to put pie menus into one of the toolkits. (I think
XView would be a good choice.) I don't have the time to do that right
now myself, but if you or anybody you know would like to work on
something like that, I'd be glad to send you the generic pie menu
algorithms I've salvaged from uwm, and answer any questions and help
out as much as time permits!

