To play with pie menus:

Make your own directory "~/tnt/win".
Copy the files "~hopkins/tnt/win/{pie,tab,winit}.ps" into your
directory.
Put "(tnt/win/winit.ps) LoadFile pop" into your .user.ps file
to load tab windows and pie menus automatically on startup,
or go "psh pie.ps" then "psh tab.ps" to load them by hand after
starting up. If you have them loaded automatically, the first jet you
bring up will use them. Otherwise jet will keep using regular window
frames. 

Once you have them loaded you can go:

psh -i
/demo ClassTabWindow send

to get some demo tab windows to play around with.
The tab windows have pie menus bound to the right button on their frames. 
Pie menus are a separate toolkit componant from the tab windows that
can be used in applications. They have a similar API to regular menus, 
but they don't replace them automatically. 

