Hi.  Thanks for the stuff you sent.  The source of this interest in pie
menus is some discussions I've been having with another intern here,
Barry Hayes, who says he remembers you from a Usenix conference.

We intend to send you a fuller reply to your message about encouraging
users to take advantage of gestures more, but haven't quite formulated
one yet.  Right now we'd like to see how the stuff you've done with pie
menus compares to the stuff we've been thinking about, which is why I
was pleased to receive your code.

I haven't, however, been able to get much of it to work.  For one thing,
I think I'm running NeWS 2.?, which seems to have some slight
differences in the PostScript interpreter from NeWS 1.1 (for which the
code you sent me claims it was written).  For example, 1.1 must have had
lazy type conversion (1.0 --> 1) because we've been getting all kinds of
type errors of this sort.  idiv no longer accepts 360.0 as an integer.

A few small modifications fixed this sufficiently that we were able to
pop up the menu in precision.ps.  That's a neat idea.  But we haven't
managed to get anything else working.  How are all these files supposed
to interact?  olwm (OpenLook) doesn't seem to pay much attention to the
installation of pie menus, and I'm not enough of a Display PostScript
hacker to write a sample application.  (All my previous work has been
with regular, printing PostScript.)

Any hints or tips would be appreciated.  As you might have guessed we're
running all this on a SparcStation under OpenWindows NeWS/X11.

Thanks a lot (and best wishes for the holidays),

         -- Aaron



